<!-- A preliminary draft of this preview was written by Siddhi Wakdikar after the 2024 Doenet workshop -->

<p>
  A student with a third floor dormitory window <m>32</m> feet off the ground tosses a water balloon straight up in the air with an initial velocity of <m>16</m> feet per second.  The instantaneous velocity of the water balloon is given by <m>v(t) = -32t + 16</m>, where <m>v</m> is measured in feet per second and <m>t</m> is measured in seconds.

    <ol marker="a.">
      <li>
        <p>
          Let <m>s(t)</m> represent the height of the water balloon above ground at time <m>t</m>, and note that <m>s</m> is an antiderivative of <m>v</m>.  That is, <m>v</m> is the derivative of <m>s</m>: <m>s'(t) = v(t)</m>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Find a formula for <m>s(t)</m> that satisfies the initial condition that the balloon is tossed from 32 feet above ground.  In other words, make your formula for <m>s</m> satisfy <m>s(0) = 32</m>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <answer name="a1"><label><m>s(t) = </m></label>-16t^2 + 16t + 32</answer>
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <p>
          When does the water balloon reach its maximum height?
        </p>
        <p sectionWideCheckWork>
          <answer name="a2"><label><m>t=</m></label>0.5</answer>seconds
        </p>
        <p>
          When does the water balloon land?
        </p>
        <p sectionWideCheckWork>
          <answer name="a3"><label><m>t=</m></label>2</answer>seconds
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <p>
          Compute each of the following quantities:</p>

        <p>
          <answer name="a4"><label><m>s(\frac{1}{2}) - s(0) = </m> </label>4</answer>
        </p>
        <p>
          <answer name="a5"><label><m>s(2)-s(\frac{1}{2}) = </m> </label>-36</answer>
        </p>
        <p>
          <answer name="a6"><label><m>s(2) - s(0) = </m> </label>-32</answer>
        </p>
          <p>
            Complete the following sentence to explain the meaning of each of these quantities.
          </p>
        <p>
          Since <m>s(t)</m> represents the height of a falling object, the quantity <m>s(b) - s(a)</m> represents the object's <answer><choiceInput inline><shortDescription>meaning of s of b minus s of a</shortDescription>
            <choice>?</choice>
            <choice>average velocity on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice>vertical distance traveled on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice credit="1">change in height on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice>average acceleration on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
          </choiceInput></answer>, which is measured in <answer><choiceInput inline><shortDescription>units of the quantity s of b minus s of a</shortDescription>
            <choice>?</choice>
            <choice>feet per second</choice>
            <choice>seconds</choice>
            <choice credit="1">feet</choice>
            <choice>feet per second per second</choice>
          </choiceInput></answer>.
        </p>
      </li>


      <li>
        <p>
          What is the total vertical distance traveled by the water balloon from the time it is tossed until the time it lands?
        </p>
        <p>
          <answer name="a7"><shortDescription>total vertical distance traveled by the balloon</shortDescription>40</answer>
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <p>
          By dragging the two points in the figure below appropriately, plot the graph of the velocity function
          <m>y = v(t) = -32t + 16</m> on the time interval <m>[0,2]</m>.
        </p>
        <graph xmin='-0.2' xmax='2.4' ymin = '-60' ymax = '40' fixAxes="true" showNavigation="false"><shortDescription>graph of velocity function</shortDescription>
          <xLabel>t</xLabel>
          <yLabel>v</yLabel>

          <setup>
            <function name = 'v'>-32x+16</function>
            <line name = 'x0'>x=0</line>
            <line name = 'x2'>x=2.00</line>
          </setup>

          <point name = "C">(0,-18)
              <constrainTo>$x0</constrainTo>
              <attractTo threshold=".4">
                <point>(0,16)</point>
              </attractTo>
          </point>

          <point name = "D">(2,-18)
              <constrainTo>$x2</constrainTo>
              <attractTo threshold=".4">
                <point>(2,-48)</point>
              </attractTo>
          </point>

          <line name = "line" through = "$C $D" />
        </graph>

        <answer><award matchPartial><when>($C, $D) = (<point>(0,16)</point>,<point>(2,-48)</point>)
        </when></award></answer>

      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          By using a familiar geometric formula to compute areas of relevant regions, find the total net-signed area bounded by
          <m>y = v(t)</m> and the <m>t</m>-axis on <m>[0,2]</m>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <label for="$a8">The total net-signed area's numerical value is </label>
        <answer name="a8">-32</answer>
        </p>
        <p>
          The meaning of the total net-signed area bounded by
          <m>y = v(t)</m> and the <m>t</m>-axis on <m>[0,2]</m> is the water balloon's <answer><choiceInput inline><shortDescription>meaning of the net-signed area</shortDescription>
            <choice>?</choice>
            <choice>average velocity on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice>vertical distance traveled on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice credit="1">change in height on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
            <choice>average acceleration on <m>[a,b]</m></choice>
          </choiceInput></answer>, which is the same as the value of <answer><choiceInput inline><shortDescription>calculation equivalent to the net-signed area between the velocity and the x axis</shortDescription>
            <choice>?</choice>
            <choice><m>\frac{s(2)-s(0)}{(2-0)}</m></choice>
            <choice credit="1"><m>s(2)-s(0)</m></choice>
            <choice><m>v(2)-v(0)</m></choice>
            <choice><m>\frac{v(2)-v(0)}{(2-0)}</m></choice>
          </choiceInput></answer> that we computed in (c).
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
</p>
